From: omaflake contributors
Subject: cocoa: a loading image until the guest's own picture

With OMAFLAKE_LOADING_IMAGE (a PNG; set by omaf and the app) the OpenGL
window shows that image from its first frame instead of the firmware's
screen, and keeps it until the guest sets a scanout of its own after the
firmware's ended (the kernel took over the GPU): its boot splash or its
console. Then the image fades out in 300 ms. Without such a scanout within
60 s it fades anyway. The image is the first frame of the guest's boot
splash, so the window shows one picture from start to splash.

